{"id":"mahabharata-5-175","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":175,"title":"पञ्चसप्तत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 175 · Akritavrana and Parashurama","summary":{"en":"Hotravahana tells Amba that Parashurama, his friend, will help her. Akritavrana, Parashurama's companion, arrives, hears the story, and Amba asks to do whatever Parashurama advises.","kn":"ತನ್ನ ಮಿತ್ರ ಪರಶುರಾಮನು ಸಹಾಯ ಮಾಡುವನೆಂದು ಹೋತ್ರವಾಹನನು ಅಂಬೆಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಪರಶುರಾಮನ ಸಂಗಡಿಗ ಅಕೃತವ್ರಣನು ಬಂದು ಕಥೆ ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಪರಶುರಾಮನು ಹೇಳಿದಂತೆ ಮಾಡುವೆನೆಂದು ಅಂಬೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"होत्रवाहन अम्बा से कहते हैं कि उनके मित्र परशुराम उसकी सहायता करेंगे। परशुराम के साथी अकृतव्रण आकर कथा सुनते हैं, और अम्बा कहती है कि परशुराम जो सलाह दें वही करेगी।","te":"తన మిత్రుడు పరశురాముడు సహాయం చేస్తాడని హోత్రవాహనుడు అంబకు చెబుతాడు. పరశురాముని సహచరుడు అకృతవ్రణుడు వచ్చి కథ వింటాడు; పరశురాముడు చెప్పినట్లు చేస్తానని అంబ అంటుంది.","ta":"தன் நண்பர் பரஶுராமர் உதவுவார் என்று ஹோத்ரவாஹனன் அம்பையிடம் சொல்கிறான். பரஶுராமரின் தோழர் அக்ருதவ்ரணர் வந்து கதையைக் கேட்க, பரஶுராமர் அறிவுறுத்துவதையே செய்வேன் என்கிறாள் அம்பை.","ml":"തന്റെ സുഹൃത്തായ പരശുരാമൻ അവളെ സഹായിക്കുമെന്ന് ഹോത്രവാഹനൻ അംബയോട് പറയുന്നു. പരശുരാമന്റെ കൂട്ടുകാരനായ അകൃതവ്രണൻ എത്തി കഥ കേൾക്കുന്നു; പരശുരാമൻ ഉപദേശിക്കുന്നതെന്തും ചെയ്യാൻ തയ്യാറാണെന്ന് അംബ പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.175; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"अम्बोपाख्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Ambopakhyana Parva (The story of Amba)","verses":[{"text":"होत्रवाहन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Hotravahana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"रामं द्रक्ष्यसि वत्से त्वं जामदग्न्यं महावने ।\nउग्रे तपसि वर्तन्तं सत्यसंधं महाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You will see Rama, son of Jamadagni, my daughter, in the great forest, practicing fierce austerity, true to his word and very strong."}},{"n":2,"text":"महेन्द्रे वै गिरिश्रेष्ठे रामं नित्यमुपासते ।\nऋषयो वेदविदुषो गन्धर्वाप्सरसस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"On Mahendra, best of mountains, sages who know the Veda, gandharvas and apsaras always attend on Rama."}},{"n":3,"text":"तत्र गच्छस्व भद्रं ते ब्रूयाश्चैनं वचो मम ।\nअभिवाद्य पूर्वं शिरसा तपोवृद्धं दृढव्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Go there, may it be well with you, and give him my message; first bow your head to that firm-vowed man, old in austerity."}},{"n":4,"text":"ब्रूयाश्चैनं पुनर्भद्रे यत्ते कार्यं मनीषितम् ।\nमयि संकीर्तिते रामः सर्वं तत्ते करिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then tell him, good lady, the task you intend; when I am named, Rama will do it all for you."}},{"n":5,"text":"मम रामः सखा वत्से प्रीतियुक्तः सुहृच्च मे ।\nजमदग्निसुतो वीरः सर्वशस्त्रभृतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama is my friend, dear one, affectionate and well-disposed, that hero, son of Jamadagni, best of all weapon-bearers."}},{"n":6,"text":"एवं ब्रुवति कन्यां तु पार्थिवे होत्रवाहने ।\nअकृतव्रणः प्रादुरासीद्रामस्यानुचरः प्रियः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While King Hotravahana was speaking thus to the maiden, Akritavrana, Rama's dear attendant, appeared."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततस्ते मुनयः सर्वे समुत्तस्थुः सहस्रशः ।\nस च राजा वयोवृद्धः सृञ्जयो होत्रवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all those sages rose by the thousands, and that aged king, the Srinjaya Hotravahana, did too."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततः पृष्ट्वा यथान्यायमन्योन्यं ते वनौकसः ।\nसहिता भरतश्रेष्ठ निषेदुः परिवार्य तम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having greeted one another as is proper, those forest dwellers sat down together around him, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":9,"text":"ततस्ते कथयामासुः कथास्तास्ता मनोरमाः ।\nकान्ता दिव्याश्च राजेन्द्र प्रीतिहर्षमुदा युताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They told those charming, lovely, divine tales, full of affection, joy and delight."}},{"n":10,"text":"ततः कथान्ते राजर्षिर्महात्मा होत्रवाहनः ।\nरामं श्रेष्ठं महर्षीणामपृच्छदकृतव्रणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At the end of the tales the royal sage, great-souled Hotravahana, asked Akritavrana, chief of Rama's sages:"}},{"n":11,"text":"क्व संप्रति महाबाहो जामदग्न्यः प्रतापवान् ।\nअकृतव्रण शक्यो वै द्रष्टुं वेदविदां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Where now, mighty-armed Akritavrana, is the glorious son of Jamadagni, best of Veda-knowers? Can he be seen?"}},{"text":"अकृतव्रण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Akritavrana said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"भवन्तमेव सततं रामः कीर्तयति प्रभो ।\nसृञ्जयो मे प्रियसखो राजर्षिरिति पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rama always speaks of you, lord: \"The royal sage Srinjaya is my dear friend.\""}},{"n":13,"text":"इह रामः प्रभाते श्वो भवितेति मतिर्मम ।\nद्रष्टास्येनमिहायान्तं तव दर्शनकाङ्क्षया ॥","meaning":{"en":"My thought is that Rama will be here at dawn tomorrow; you will see him come here, wishing to see you."}},{"n":14,"text":"इयं च कन्या राजर्षे किमर्थं वनमागता ।\nकस्य चेयं तव च का भवतीच्छामि वेदितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Royal sage, why has this maiden come to the forest? Whose is she, and who is she to you? I wish to know."}},{"text":"होत्रवाहन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Hotravahana said:"}},{"n":15,"text":"दौहित्रीयं मम विभो काशिराजसुता शुभा ।\nज्येष्ठा स्वयंवरे तस्थौ भगिनीभ्यां सहानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"She is my daughter's daughter, mighty one, the lovely daughter of the Kashi king, who stood in the self-choice as the eldest with her two sisters, blameless one."}},{"n":16,"text":"इयमम्बेति विख्याता ज्येष्ठा काशिपतेः सुता ।\nअम्बिकाम्बालिके त्वन्ये यवीयस्यौ तपोधन ॥","meaning":{"en":"She is called Amba, the eldest daughter of the Kashi king; Ambika and Ambalika are the other two, younger, rich in austerity."}},{"n":17,"text":"समेतं पार्थिवं क्षत्रं काशिपुर्यां ततोऽभवत् ।\nकन्यानिमित्तं ब्रह्मर्षे तत्रासीदुत्सवो महान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A gathering of kings assembled in the city of Kashi, Brahmin sage, and there was a great festival on account of the maidens."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततः किल महावीर्यो भीष्मः शांतनवो नृपान् ।\nअवाक्षिप्य महातेजास्तिस्रः कन्या जहार ताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, they say, the mighty Bhishma son of Shantanu, of great splendor, defying the kings, carried off those three maidens."}},{"n":19,"text":"निर्जित्य पृथिवीपालानथ भीष्मो गजाह्वयम् ।\nआजगाम विशुद्धात्मा कन्याभिः सह भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having defeated the kings, Bhishma of pure soul came to Hastinapura with the maidens, Bharata."}},{"n":20,"text":"सत्यवत्यै निवेद्याथ विवाहार्थमनन्तरम् ।\nभ्रातुर्विचित्रवीर्यस्य समाज्ञापयत प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He informed Satyavati, and then the lord ordered preparations for his brother Vichitravirya's wedding."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततो वैवाहिकं दृष्ट्वा कन्येयं समुपार्जितम् ।\nअब्रवीत्तत्र गाङ्गेयं मन्त्रिमध्ये द्विजर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, seeing the wedding arrangements made, this maiden spoke to Ganga's son among the ministers, best of Brahmins."}},{"n":22,"text":"मया शाल्वपतिर्वीर मनसाभिवृतः पतिः ।\nन मामर्हसि धर्मज्ञ परचित्तां प्रदापितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I had chosen the king of Shalva in my heart as my husband; you should not give me away, knower of dharma, when my heart is another's."}},{"n":23,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा वचनं भीष्मः संमन्त्र्य सह मन्त्रिभिः ।\nनिश्चित्य विससर्जेमां सत्यवत्या मते स्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing her words, Bhishma consulted with his ministers, decided, and released her, following Satyavati's opinion."}},{"n":24,"text":"अनुज्ञाता तु भीष्मेण शाल्वं सौभपतिं ततः ।\nकन्येयं मुदिता विप्र काले वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Released by Bhishma, this maiden joyfully spoke at the right time to Shalva, king of Saubha, Brahmin."}},{"n":25,"text":"विसर्जितास्मि भीष्मेण धर्मं मां प्रतिपादय ।\nमनसाभिवृतः पूर्वं मया त्वं पार्थिवर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma has released me; accept me in dharma; I chose you in my heart before, bull among kings."}},{"n":26,"text":"प्रत्याचख्यौ च शाल्वोऽपि चारित्रस्याभिशङ्कितः ।\nसेयं तपोवनं प्राप्ता तापस्येऽभिरता भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Shalva rejected her too, suspecting her conduct. Now she has come to this ascetic forest, deeply devoted to austerity."}},{"n":27,"text":"मया च प्रत्यभिज्ञाता वंशस्य परिकीर्तनात् ।\nअस्य दुःखस्य चोत्पत्तिं भीष्ममेवेह मन्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I recognized her when she told me about her lineage; and she holds Bhishma alone to be the origin of this sorrow."}},{"text":"अम्बोवाच","meaning":{"en":"Amba said:"}},{"n":28,"text":"भगवन्नेवमेवैतद्यथाह पृथिवीपतिः ।\nशरीरकर्ता मातुर्मे सृञ्जयो होत्रवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Revered one, it is just as the king says; the king Srinjaya Hotravahana is the maker of my mother's body."}},{"n":29,"text":"न ह्युत्सहे स्वनगरं प्रतियातुं तपोधन ।\nअवमानभयाच्चैव व्रीडया च महामुने ॥","meaning":{"en":"I cannot go back to my city, ascetic, from fear of contempt and from shame, great sage."}},{"n":30,"text":"यत्तु मां भगवान्रामो वक्ष्यति द्विजसत्तम ।\nतन्मे कार्यतमं कार्यमिति मे भगवन्मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever the revered Rama tells me, best of Brahmins, I think that is the thing I most must do, sir."}}]}]}